WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.650
Gate 4 starts with the rule text,
because here a rule is an access grant.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.688
Every governed group uses
one of two patterns.

3
00:00:07.688 --> 00:00:11.134
A node query selects people
by one organization code,

4
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:15.050
and uses the in operator for a
roll-up instead of a chain of ors.

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:19.523
A functional query crosses the
organization with another coded attribute,

6
00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:24.350
such as position category, to answer a
question that isn't about where someone sits.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.175
Every access rule carries two guards.

8
00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:30.745
The account must be enabled, and
the user type must be Member,

9
00:00:30.745 --> 00:00:33.513
which keeps out disabled
accounts and guests.

10
00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:36.020
An agent's user account is a kind of user,

11
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.075
so user rules include it
unless they exclude it.

12
00:00:39.075 --> 00:00:43.213
The books don't give the clause, so
prove yours with a named-user test.

13
00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:46.179
Rules read codes, never
department or job title,

14
00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:50.287
because a display string breaks
the next time someone retypes it.

15
00:00:50.287 --> 00:00:52.390
And privileged groups stay assigned.
